```js
function promiseAll(promises) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const results = [];
    let remaining = promises.length;
    if (remaining === 0) return resolve(results);
    promises.forEach((p, i) => {
      Promise.resolve(p).then((val) => {
        results[i] = val;
        if (--remaining === 0) resolve(results);
      }, reject);
    });
  });
}
```

**Spoken answer:** "A transaction groups several statements so they succeed or fail as one unit (that's Atomicity). `COMMIT` makes the changes permanent; `ROLLBACK` undoes everything since the transaction began; `SAVEPOINT` sets a marker so you can roll back *partially* to that point instead of the whole thing."

```sql
BEGIN TRANSACTION;
    UPDATE Accounts SET Balance = Balance - 100 WHERE Id = 1;
    SAVE TRANSACTION AfterDebit;         -- savepoint
    UPDATE Accounts SET Balance = Balance + 100 WHERE Id = 2;
    -- if the credit fails: ROLLBACK TRANSACTION AfterDebit;
COMMIT;
```

